   "html": "<p>The circuit shown in figure is a model for a battery charger. Here, <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/69/69fc756707526cdd396b.png\" /> is a 10 V peak sine wave, <em>D</em><sub>1 </sub>and <em>D<sub>2</sub></em> are ideal diodes, <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/4e/4e68c0e8355e361a5e61.png\" /> is 100 mA current source and <em>B</em> is a 4.5 V battery. If the peak value of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/79/7975dd3c6cb818c0536d.png\" /> is reduced by 10%, then average value of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/19/19a0eabd75fd38d95be4.png\" /> becomes _____ mA.<br />\n(Rounded off to two decimal places)</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ec/ec07fc2a88adbedd4788.png\" /></p>",
